@@ -1133,6 +1134,25 @@ At 0, the kernel will not initiate swap until the amount of free and
 file-backed pages is less than the high watermark in a zone.
 
 
+thp_direct_reclaim_split
+========================
+
+When set to 1, direct reclaim (an allocating task reclaiming memory
+itself) does not swap out a whole large anonymous folio, such as a 2 MiB
+transparent huge page, if that compresses or copies every page of it in
+the allocating task (zram and other synchronous swap devices, or zswap)
+and the task needs much less memory than that. It splits the folio,
+reclaims about as many pages as the task needs from its start, and
+leaves the rest on the LRU for kswapd. With zram and zstd this turns
+3-4 ms of compression for a 2 MiB folio into a fraction of a
+millisecond, at the cost of the split (the folio is unmapped and
+remapped) and of that huge page. kswapd, proactive reclaim
+(memory.reclaim) and MADV_PAGEOUT still swap out large folios whole.
+thp_swpout_direct_split in /proc/vmstat counts the splits.
+
+The default value is 0.
+
+
 unprivileged_userfaultfd
 ========================
 
